  message: "P4 REVIEW 2026-11-01 (dev 9ae4abe13f; owner-requested re-check of open P4 items last modified before 2026-10-20; fixtures under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/p4_review_11012026/graph1/). VERDICT: PARTLY-STALE. Review 2026-11-01 at dev 9ae4abe13f. status 'complete' was renamed 'provenance_declared' (e6cb77fa15, 2026-08-16, INV-titih), and _validate_catalog_dict (io_boundary.py:482) now refuses 'complete'. Coverage claims moved to per-module module_completeness, so audit step (1) is no longer part of the status flip. provenance_declared today: python, rust, erlang (PR #3893), javascript (e31c29a124, 2026-09-06). Still in_progress from the 12-list: c, elixir, go, haskell, java, kotlin, objc, scala, swift. cpp and bash are also in_progress but were never on the list. MECHANISM: The catalog status axis was redefined: 'complete' is now refused, 'provenance_declared' is a citation check only, and coverage moved to per-module module_completeness."  # 15ff
