js.org and developer.mozilla.org\n  [ ] kotlin   — kotlinlang.org\n  [ ] objc     — developer.apple.com\n  [ ] rust     — doc.rust-lang.org/std/\n  [ ] scala    — scala-lang.org\n  [ ] swift    — swift.org or developer.apple.com\n\nSuggested execution: ship as 1-3 PRs, batched by per-language audit effort. The audit step is the bulk of the work; the YAML declaration itself is a few lines per catalog. As each language ships, append a discussion entry checking it off.\n\nThis umbrella replaces 12 individual P3 items (WI-ganid c, WI-tumor elixir, WI-gunur erlang, WI-honir go, WI-tusof haskell, WI-vikop java, WI-fobus javascript, WI-labiz kotlin, WI-pitot objc, WI-galaz rust, WI-puzoj swift, WI-vubil scala) all created 2026-04-24 from the same template with zero discussion entries each. Discrete tracking made tracker ready noisy with 11 misleading 'P3 ready' entries that conveyed no per-item priority information. Consolidated 2026-04-27 per human direction."  # 2c23
